      "problem": "Find ${f}^{′}(x)$ for $f(x)={log}_{5}⁡x+5\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.$",
      "worked_solution": "To differentiate a logarithm with base $a,$ we use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({log}_{a}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡a}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({log}_{5}⁡x+5\\operatorname{ln}⁡x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}+5(\\frac{1}{x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}+\\frac{5}{x}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
